#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:766
msgid "How exactly should the trait for this be named and structured?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:769
msgid "Future possibilities"
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:772
msgid "Annotated heterogeneous `try` blocks"
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:774
msgid ""
"We could have `try ☃️ anyhow::Result<_> { ... }` blocks that use the old `?` "
"desugaring. (Insert your favourite token in place of ☃️, but please don't "
"discuss that in _this_ RFC.)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:777
msgid ""
"The extra token is negligible compared to the type annotation, unlike it "
"would be in the homogeneous case."
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:779
msgid ""
"That could be done at any point, as it's not a breaking change, thanks to "
"`try` being a keyword."
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:781
msgid ""
"The [flavour](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3710) conversation "
"might find a version of this that could go well with `async` blocks too."
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:783
msgid ""
"There are also other possible versions of this taking more advantage of the "
"residual type to avoid needing to write the `_` in more cases.  Spitballing, "
"you could have things like `try ☃️ Option` or `try ☃️ anyhow::Result`, say, "
"where that isn't a type but is instead a 1-parameter type _constructor_."
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:789
msgid "Integration with `yeet`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:791
msgid ""
"This RFC has no conflict with [`yeet`](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"issues/96373), though it does open up some new questions."
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:795
msgid ""
"In many ways, the discussion here is similar to an open question about "
"`yeet` around what conversions, if any, it can do."
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:798
msgid "For example, if I'm in a `-> io::Result<()>` function, can I do"
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:802
msgid "or would it need to be"
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:806
msgid "or even require full specificity?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:811
msgid ""
"One potentially-interesting version of that would be to keep `yeet` as "
"_heterogeneous_ inside the _homogeneous_ `try` blocks."
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:814
msgid ""
"That would mean that it would still be the `?`s that would pick the return "
"type, but you'd be able to `yeet` more-specific types that would get "
"translated."
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:817
msgid "For example, that could allow something like"
msgstr ""

#: src/3721-homogeneous-try-blocks.md:828
msgid ""
"where the `?`s are still homogeneous, picking `io::Result<()>` as the return "
"type for the block, but still allowing error-conversion in the `yeet` so you "
"can `yeet` the \"more specific\" type and still have the compiler figure it "
"out."
msgstr ""
